# issue 28: VACASK's capacitor takes no q=. Its grammar's `rewrite capacitor q` block writes a
# behavioural source whose current is ddt of the charge, times m; what else the capacitor gives
# (a value, a model, other parameters) has no place on it and is a loss each.
from: ngspice
to: vacask
--- input
t
C3 a 0 q='1p*v(a)' m=2
C4 b 0 q='1p*v(b)' m={2*k}
C5 b 0 1p cmod q='2p*v(b)' ic=1 tc1=1
.model cmod c
.tran 1n 5n
.end
--- output
t
ground 0
load "spice/capacitor.osdi"
model capacitor sp_capacitor
c3 (a 0) i=2*ddt(1p*v(a))
c4 (b 0) i=(2*k)*ddt(1p*v(b))
c5 (b 0) i=ddt(2p*v(b))
model cmod sp_capacitor
control
analysis tran1 tran step=1n stop=5n maxstep=1n
endc
--- report
error[invalid]: line 2: node 'a' has no DC path to ground: only C3 reaches it, which conducts no DC there; VACASK's operating point fails on it, where ngspice gets through with its transient operating point; a large resistor to ground gives one
error[invalid]: line 3: node 'b' has no DC path to ground: only C4, C5 reach it, which conduct no DC there; VACASK's operating point fails on it, where ngspice gets through with its transient operating point; a large resistor to ground gives one
info[oneway]: line 2: capacitor 'C3': vacask's capacitor takes no charge (q=); it is written as a behavioural source whose current is 2*ddt(1e-12*v(a)), which reads back as that source
info[rename]: line 2: renamed 'C3' to 'c3': vacask finds it only in lower case
info[oneway]: line 3: capacitor 'C4': vacask's capacitor takes no charge (q=); it is written as a behavioural source whose current is (2*k)*ddt(1e-12*v(b)), which reads back as that source
info[rename]: line 3: renamed 'C4' to 'c4': vacask finds it only in lower case
error[loss]: line 4: capacitor 'C5': 'c=1p' has no place on the behavioural source a capacitor given by its charge is written as for vacask
error[loss]: line 4: capacitor 'C5': the model 'cmod' has no place on the behavioural source a capacitor given by its charge is written as for vacask
error[loss]: line 4: capacitor 'C5': 'ic=1' has no place on the behavioural source a capacitor given by its charge is written as for vacask
error[loss]: line 4: capacitor 'C5': 'tc1=1' has no place on the behavioural source a capacitor given by its charge is written as for vacask
info[oneway]: line 4: capacitor 'C5': vacask's capacitor takes no charge (q=); it is written as a behavioural source whose current is ddt(2e-12*v(b)), which reads back as that source
info[rename]: line 4: renamed 'C5' to 'c5': vacask finds it only in lower case
warning[synthesized]: line 6: tran: vacask needs 'maxstep' to behave as ngspice does without it; wrote 1n
